  #line-at(57.36pt, 238.34pt, "Abstract ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 269.21pt, "All-electrical methods for nucleating, detecting, and manipulating spin textures in two-dimensional ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 289.37pt, "(2D) van der Waals (vdW) magnets can serve as fundamental building blocks for multi-state ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 309.53pt, "spintronic memory, logic, and neuromorphic computing applications. Unlike conventional ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 329.57pt, "ferromagnets, vdW ferromagnet such as Fe₅GeTe₂ with strong Dzyaloshinskii-Moriya interactions ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 349.73pt, "stabilize nanoscale chiral spin textures including skyrmions and stripe domains.  However, the sub-")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 369.89pt, "100 nm size of these spin textures has limited their study to sophisticated microscopy techniques. ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 390.05pt, "Here, we demonstrate all-electrical detection of spin textures in vdW itinerant ferromagnet Fe₅GeTe₂ ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 410.21pt, "using pure spin transport in a lateral graphene spin-valve device at room temperature. By engineering ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 430.39pt, "nanoscale constrictions or notches in Fe₅GeTe₂, we create spin textures that inject distinct spin ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 450.55pt, "polarizations into the graphene channel, where they are nonlocally sensed by a reference ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 470.59pt, "conventional ferromagnetic detector at room temperature. This enables the observation of ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 490.75pt, "anomalous multi-level spin-valve switching and Hanle spin precession signals, which are due to ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 510.91pt, "unique spin textures in Fe₅GeTe₂ and in sharp contrast to single-domains and conventional magnet-")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 531.07pt, "based devices. This all-electrical approach can provide direct access to the spin textures on an ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 551.23pt, "integrated 2D spintronic circuit without the need for ex-situ microscopic characterizations. ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 665.74pt, "Keywords: ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(112.22pt, 665.74pt, "spin texture, 2D magnets, electrical detection method, graphene, spin circuit")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(57.36pt, 693.096pt, "Corresponding author:")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(170.66pt, 693.096pt, " Email: saroj.dash@chalmers.se")
]

