  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(57.36pt, 82.34pt, "Conclusion and Outlook ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(57.36pt, 109.82pt, "Our electrical detection of spin texture in Fe₅GeTe₂ reveals fundamental aspects of magnetism in van der ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 129.98pt, "Waals materials that distinguish them from conventional ferromagnets. As Fe₅GeTe₂ is known to exhibit ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 150.02pt, "stronger DMI than conventional ferromagnets, a simple notch and constriction can nucleate complex chiral ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 170.18pt, "spin configurations including skyrmions and stripe domains. We introduced an all-electrical method for ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 190.34pt, "detecting such spin textures in Fe₅GeTe₂using pure spin transport in a graphene-based lateral spin-valve ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 210.5pt, "device. By engineering constrictions or notches in Fe₅GeTe₂, we created robust spin textures, which were ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 230.66pt, "injected into and electrically detected through a graphene channel at room temperature. This work marks ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 250.82pt, "the first demonstration of graphene as a spin transport channel for sensing spin textures in vdW magnets, ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 270.89pt, "enabling multi-level spin valve switching and Hanle precession signals without reliance on conventionally ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 291.05pt, "used microscopy techniques. The methodology established here for FGT can be extended to other 2D ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 311.21pt, "magnets with varying DMI strengths to understand how DMI emerge from crystal symmetry breaking in ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 331.37pt, "reduced dimensions. Such studies could guide the design of voltage-tunable spin textures in 2D ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 351.53pt, "heterostructures, where electrostatic gating can modulate DMI and stabilize different topological states on ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 371.69pt, "demand. The ability to detect complex spin textures in a simple 2D heterostructure by all-electrical methods ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 391.85pt, "can pave the way for the design of programmable spin logic elements and neuromorphic architectures")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(549.1pt, 387.89pt, "[66]")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(559.78pt, 391.85pt, ". ")
  #line-at(57.36pt, 411.89pt, "Our approach stands apart from existing magnetic tunnel junction")
